xdg-user-dirs

# --- input methods (CJK) ----------------------------------------------------
# Sky1 is a Chinese SoC with an expected domestic user base, and this project
# ships bilingual EN/zh-CN documentation, so Chinese input is a first-class
# requirement rather than an afterthought.
#
# The fonts were already here (fonts-noto-cjk above); what was missing was any
# way to TYPE the characters they render. The shipped labwc implements the
# text-input and input-method protocols (verified: get_input_method,
# get_text_input, handle_text_input_commit are all present in the binary), so
# fcitx5 has a compositor to talk to on Wayland.
#
# Closure measured against forky arm64: 25 packages, ~45 MB of .debs, 0
# removals. Against a 3.4 GB install image that is +1.3%.
#
# These are installed unconditionally; whether an IME AUTOSTARTS is decided at
# install time by the language selection (see post-install/22-locale-gen.sh).
# Shipping the packages and not enabling them costs 45 MB; NOT shipping them
# means a Chinese user cannot type on a fully offline install, which is the
# whole point of an offline installer.
fcitx5
fcitx5-chinese-addons
fcitx5-config-qt
im-config

# --- browser + media -------------------------------------------------------
# Vivaldi installs from the staged upstream .deb in 52-vivaldi.sh and remains
# the default browser. Real, official Google Chrome for arm64 Linux (public
# since Q2 2026, via Google's own signed apt repo) is the second browser —
# build-desktop-mirror folds it into the offline desktop pool, pinned +
# SHA256-verified against Google's published Packages index; no live apt
# source on the shipped image, no snapd. ungoogled-chromium/XtraDeb (an
# earlier stop-gap from before real Chrome existed for arm64) is dropped —
# real Chrome supersedes it outright.
# chromium-ncz-sky1 is OUR Chromium build (V4L2-M2M hardware decode, which no
# upstream or distro arm64 build provides on Sky1). It is the default browser
# and is pinned on the launcher alongside Chrome and the terminal, but it was
# neither seeded here nor present in the forky mirror -- so the launcher would
# have pinned a browser the image never installed.
chromium-ncz-sky1
google-chrome-stable
mpv
# crash traceability for the desktop session (post-install/20-desktop.sh diagnostics;
# r201: it was unseeded, so the hook installed nothing while claiming success)
systemd-coredump
# nspawn runtime for the recovery container (post-install/38-recovery-container.sh);
# r201: unseeded, so the hook's apt-get install failed rc=100 on arm64
systemd-container
# NOE_Engine imports numpy at module scope (post-install/25-cix-proprietary.sh, Sky1 only);
# r201: unseeded, so its apt-get install failed rc=100 and the NPU python path was left without numpy
python3-numpy

